steps.prompt_template:
You are reviewing a change you did not write.

Under review: {{feature_description}}
Branch: {{feature_branch}}
Repositories in scope: {{repo_list}}
Project conventions: {{project_conventions}}

## How to review

That is yours to decide, not Demeteo's. Use your own review capability — a built-in review command, a skill, a subagent, or simply reading — and judge the change against what this project has written down about itself: the conventions above, and whatever `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` or contributing guide the repository carries.

{{review_entrypoint}}

## Where the report goes

`artifacts/code-review.md`. That file is the whole deliverable, and it is also the only path you may write to — the source tree is read-only for this step.

A second step follows yours: the orchestrator runs this project's own preparation and gate commands on this branch, so whether the branch builds is answered beside your report rather than in it. Where those gates pass, none is configured, or every failure among them pre-dates the branch, that step writes what they said to `artifacts/branch-validation.md`. A gate this branch turned red ends the step before any agent turn in `s-validate-branch`: no `branch-validation.md` is written, and the failing command's output is recorded as the step's failure reason instead. Neither step commits, pushes, squashes or opens a pull request. A human reads what both leave behind and decides what happens to the change.

## Stop condition
You are done when `artifacts/code-review.md` exists and speaks to the range above.
